The Servicemembers Civil Relief Act (SCRA) provides legal and financial protections to those who have answered the Nation's call to serve. Download our fact sheet to learn more. The 6 percent interest rate cap applies to: auto loans, mortgages, credit cards, other installment loans, and student loans taken out after August 14, 2008. The SCRA also applies to loans that you and your spouse took out together. In order to qualify for the 6 percent interest rate cap, you must:
Currently be in active-duty military service;
Have taken out the loan before entering active-duty military service;
Notify your lender in writing and include a copy of your military orders calling you to active duty.

